    'Classic FUO (Petersdorf and Beeson, modified) is fever above 38.3°C on several occasions over at least 3 weeks with no diagnosis after a defined set of investigations (e.g., 3 outpatient visits, 3 days in hospital or 1 week of intelligent investigation). The main categories are infections (TB — especially extrapulmonary in India — abscesses, endocarditis, enteric fever, brucellosis), malignancies (lymphoma, leukaemia, renal cell carcinoma), non-infectious inflammatory diseases (adult-onset Still disease, giant cell arteritis, SLE) and miscellaneous (drug fever, factitious fever). Separate categories exist for nosocomial, neutropenic and HIV-associated FUO.',
